":"Byzantine Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Milutin","c":2},{"y":1284,"t":"split","x":"1284: Dragutin's separate kingdom, agreed with the Syrmia dossier's found event of 1284.","cp":"kingdom-of-syrmia","cpn":"Kingdom of Syrmia","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Dragutin","c":2},{"y":1296,"t":"gain","x":"1296: Milutin takes Durrës.","cp":"byzantine-empire","cpn":"Byzantine Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Milutin","c":2},{"y":1299,"t":"contest_end","x":"1299: peace with Byzantium.","cp":"byzantine-empire","cpn":"Byzantine Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Milutin","c":3},{"y":1299,"t":"capital_move","x":"1299: Skopje becomes the capital.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serbian_Kingdom_(medieval)","c":2},{"y":1301,"t":"gain","x":"1301: Milutin takes Rudnik.","cp":"kingdom-of-syrmia","cpn":"Kingdom of Syrmia","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Dragutin","c":3},{"y":1304,"t":"loss","x":"1304: Durrës is Angevin again.","cp":"house-of-anjou-sicily","cpn":"House of Anjou-Sicily","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Albania_(medieval)","c":3},{"y":1312,"t":"loss","x":"c. 1312: Rudnik returns to Dragutin. Milutin defeated Dragutin in 'late 1311 or 1312' and 'the prelates mediated a peace treaty between them most probably in 1312'; Dragutin's 'Serbian appanage (including the silver mine at Rudnik) was fully restored to him'. Mirror of kingdom-of-syrmia /ledger/4; keyframe _1312 draws…","cp":"kingdom-of-syrmia","cpn":"Kingdom of Syrmia","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Dragutin","c":2},{"y":1316,"t":"gain","x":"1316: Milutin takes Dragutin's lands.","cp":"kingdom-of-syrmia","cpn":"Kingdom of Syrmia","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Milutin","c":3},{"y":1319,"t":"loss","x":"1319: Hungary retakes Belgrade and Mačva.","cp":"kingdom-of-hungary","cpn":"Kingdom of Hungary","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Milutin","c":3},{"y":1321,"t":"loss","x":"1321: Vladislav II is restored to Syrmia after Milutin's death.","cp":"kingdom-of-syrmia","cpn":"Kingdom of Syrmia","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Vladislav_II","c":2},{"y":1323,"t":"contest_start","x":"1323: war with Vladislav II over Dragutin's lands.","cp":"kingdom-of-syrmia","cpn":"Kingdom of Syrmia","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_De%C4%8Danski","c":3},{"y":1324,"t":"contest_end","x":"1324: Vladislav II is beaten.","cp":"kingdom-of-syrmia","cpn":"Kingdom of Syrmia","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_De%C4%8Danski","c":3},{"y":1324,"t":"gain","x":"1324: Dečanski absorbs the Syrmian lands except Belgrade and Mačva, which Hungary has held since 1319.","cp":"kingdom-of-syrmia","cpn":"Kingdom of Syrmia","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_De%C4%8Danski","c":2},{"y":1326,"t":"loss","x":"1326: Bosnia takes Hum.","cp":"banate-of-bosnia","cpn":"Banate of Bosnia","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_De%C4%8Danski","c":3},{"y":1329,"t":"loss","x":"1329: Nevesinje and Zagorje pass to Bosnia.","cp":"banate-of-bosnia","cpn":"Banate of Bosnia","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Du%C5%A1an","c":2},{"y":1331,"t":"contest_start","x":"1331: the Macedonian war begins.","cp":"byzantine-empire","cpn":"Byzantine Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serbian_Kingdom_(medieval)","c":2},{"y":1333,"t":"loss","x":"1333: Dušan sells Ston and Pelješac.","cp":"republic-of-ragusa","cpn":"Republic of Ragusa","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Du%C5%A1an","c":3},{"y":1334,"t":"contest_end","x":"26 August 1334: peace with Byzantium.","m":8,"cp":"byzantine-empire","cpn":"Byzantine Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Du%C5%A1an","c":3},{"y":1334,"t":"gain","x":"26 August 1334: Dušan keeps Ohrid, Prilep, Strumica and the forts of the Struma.","m":8,"cp":"byzantine-empire","cpn":"Byzantine Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Du%C5%A1an","c":3},{"y":1335,"t":"gain","x":"1335: Dušan takes Belgrade and Mačva.","cp":"kingdom-of-hungary","cpn":"Kingdom of Hungary","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Du%C5%A1an","c":3},{"y":1342,"t":"contest_start","x":"1342: Dušan's offensive in the Byzantine civil war.","cp":"byzantine-empire","cpn":"Byzantine Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Du%C5%A1an","c":2},{"y":1345,"t":"gain","x":"1345: Macedonia as far as Kavala is Serbian.","cp":"byzantine-empire","cpn":"Byzantine Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Du%C5%A1an","c":2},{"y":1345,"t":"gain","x":"25 September 1345: Serres falls.","m":9,"cp":"byzantine-empire","cpn":"Byzantine Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Du%C5%A1an","c":3},{"y":1345,"t":"contest_end","x":"1345: the kingdom's part of the war ends with Serres; the conquests of Epirus and Thessaly (1347-1348) belong to the serbian-empire dossier.","m":9,"cp":"byzantine-empire","cpn":"Byzantine Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Du%C5%A1an","c":2},{"y":1346,"t":"dissolve","x":"16 April 1346: Dušan is crowned Emperor at Skopje.","m":4,"cp":"serbian-empire","cpn":"Serbian Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Du%C5%A1an","c":3}],"wars":[{"name":"Nemanja's war with Byzantium and the Battle of the South Morava","from":1188,"to":1193,"outcome":"Nemanja, allied with Béla III in 1183, attacked Byzantium, met Barbarossa at Niš in July 1189, took Skopje's direction in 1190 and was defeated by Isaac II on the South Morava (1191); the peace of 1193 had Stefan marry a Byzantine princess.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Nemanja"},{"name":"Bulgarian invasion of Serbia and the brothers' war","from":1202,"to":1205,"outcome":"Vukan drove Stefan out in 1202 (to Kaloyan); Stefan returned in 1204 and the brothers' fighting stopped in 1205; Kaloyan took Niš in 1203.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_the_First-Crowned"},{"name":"Serbo-Ragusan war (1252-1254)","from":1252,"to":1254,"outcome":"'In 1252-1253, Uroš I was at war with the Republic of Ragusa' (allied with Bulgaria); 'Peace was ensured in a charter dated May 22, 1254.'","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Uro%C5%A1_I"},{"name":"Serbian invasion of Mačva (1268)","from":1268,"to":1268,"outcome":"Uroš I invaded the Hungarian possessions in Mačva, was captured and paid for his release.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Uro%C5%A1_I"},{"name":"Dragutin's revolt (1276)","from":1276,"to":1276,"outcome":"Dragutin demanded the throne in 1276 and, with Hungarian help, Uroš abdicated and retired to Hum; Dragutin abdicated for Milutin in 1282 and became King of Srem.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Uro%C5%A1_I"},{"name":"Milutin's Macedonian war with Byzantium","from":1282,"to":1299,"outcome":"Milutin took northern Macedonia and Skopje in 1282, reached Kavala in 1283 and kept the conquests in the 1299 peace as the dowry of Simonis; Skopje became the capital.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Milutin"},{"name":"War between Dečanski and Vladislav II","from":1323,"to":1324,"outcome":"Rudnik was held by Dečanski's officials by the end of 1323; Vladislav was beaten in late 1324 and fled to Hungary.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_De%C4%8Danski"},{"name":"Bosnian conquest of Hum (1326)","from":1326,"to":1326,"outcome":"'By the end of the same year, Serbia lost the region of Hum to Bosnia.'","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_De%C4%8Danski"},{"name":"Battle of Velbazhd (1330)","from":1330,"to":1330,"outcome":"Dečanski 'defeated and killed Michael Asen III in the Battle of Velbazhd (1330)'; Bulgaria lost no land (Velbazhd page, opened for the Bulgarian dossier) and Serbia advanced in Macedonia.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_De%C4%8Danski"},{"name":"Dušan's Macedonian war (1331-1334)","from":1331,"to":1334,"outcome":"Peace of 26 August 1334: the Byzantines recognised Serbian gains in Ohrid, Prilep, Strumitsa, Siderokastron, Chermen and Prosek.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Du%C5%A1an"},{"name":"Dušan's offensive in the Byzantine civil war","from":1342,"to":1346,"outcome":"Macedonia as far as Kavala without Thessaloniki; Serres on 25 September 1345; Dušan crowned Emperor at Skopje on 16 April 1346.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Du%C5%A1an"}],"certainty":[{"from":1188,"to":1346,"level":"soft","note":"Medieval frontiers of the Nemanjić state are approximate throughout."}],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serbian_Kingdom_(medieval)","title":"Serbian Kingdom (medieval) (Kingdom of Serbia, 1217-1346)"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_the_First-Crowned","title":"Stefan the First-Crowned"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Uro%C5%A1_I","title":"Stefan Uroš I"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Milutin","title":"Stefan Milutin"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_De%C4%8Danski","title":"Stefan Dečanski"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Du%C5%A1an","title":"Stefan Dušan"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Nemanja","title":"Stefan Nemanja"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Serbia","title":"Kingdom of Serbia (1882-1918)"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Bulgarian_Empire","title":"Second Bulgarian Empire"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skopje","title":"Skopje"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ni%C5%A1","title":"Niš"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Vladislav","title":"Stefan Vladislav"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Dragutin","title":"Stefan Dragutin"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Vladislav_II","title":"Stefan Vladislav II"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivan_Asen_II_of_Bulgaria","title":"Ivan Asen II of Bulgaria"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prizren","title":"Prizren"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vukan_Nemanji%C4%87","title":"Vukan Nemanjić"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zachlumia","title":"Zachlumia"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Albania_(medieval)","title":"Kingdom of Albania (medieval)"}]}